{"files": {"SKILL.md": "## Implementation Workflow Guide\n\n### 1) Before writing code\n- Review available documentation, task details, and prior records first.\n- Implement the request as written; do not add interpretation or extra scope.\n\n### 2) While changing code\n- Keep edits focused and limited to the specified target.\n- Prefer proven patterns from existing working code over new designs.\n- Preserve current correct behavior while introducing the change.\n\n### 3) Tool usage\n- Use one chained terminal command when steps depend on each other.\n- Read the complete file before editing.\n\n### 4) Validation and closeout\n- Run applicable checks and trust observed results over assumptions.\n- Act with strict expected outcomes, test to confirm those expectations, and fix immediately when results differ.\n- Re-check the modified target after each meaningful update.\n- Keep communication short and clear.\n- If a persistent notes location exists, add a brief generalized takeaway.\n"}, "schema_version": 1}